allium-inspect calls allium's own parser and analyser as a library rather than
reimplementing them, so the binaries built from this repository contain that
code. The MIT License requires its copyright notice to travel with it, which is
what this file is for: ship it alongside any binary you distribute.

The `allium` command-line tool is a separate program. allium-inspect runs it for
two of its commands and does not include it.

Every other dependency comes from crates.io under the terms `cargo deny check
licenses` enforces; run `just deny` for the current list.
